    "dataProcessingProtocol": "MS data were processed using MaxQuant v1.6 with the MaxLFQ algorithm. The acquired spectra were searched against a rice protein database (149,216 entries), with precursor and fragment mass tolerances set at 20 ppm. The main search peptide tolerance was set at 4.5 ppm based on instrument characteristics. Oxidation of methionine (+15.995 Da) and N-terminal acetylation were set as variable modifications, whereas trypsin was specified as the cleavage enzyme with a maximum of two missed cleavages. An FDR of 1% was applied at the peptide level, and label-free quantification (LFQ) was done with the “match between runs” feature enabled.",
