    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Two-week-old hydroponically grown rice plants were treated with 150 mM NaCl applied to the roots via the cultivation solution. Leaf samples were collected at 0 h (control), and after 1 h, 3 h, 6 h, and 12 h of NaCl treatment. Each time point included three biological replicates. Rice leaves samples were immediately frozen in liquid nitrogen, and ground into a fine powder. The powdered tissue was transferred to 10 mL centrifuge tubes for protein extraction. Proteins were extracted by adding four volumes of lysis buffer containing 8 M urea, 2 mM EDTA, 0.5% Triton X-100, 1% protease inhibitor cocktail, 200 U/mL catalase, and 100 mM Tris-HCl (pH 7.2). The lysates were incubated on ice for 20 min, followed by an additional 20 min incubation at room temperature with continuous vortex mixing at 400 rpm. Insoluble debris was removed by centrifugation at 12,000 rpm for 10 min at 4 ℃, and the supernatants were collected. Protein concentrations were determined using a bicinchoninic acid (BCA) protein assay kit (Vazyme, Nanjing, China). Protein extracts were incubated with 33 µM NM-biotin (Pierce) in the dark at room temperature for 1 h to alkylate both the cysteine thiols and persulfides. The alkylated proteome were precipitated with ice-cold acetone, and washed 3 times with ice-cold acetone to remove excess NM-biotin. The resulting protein pellets were dissolved in denaturation buffer (8 M urea, 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 8). Protein concentration was determined using bicinchoninic acid assay (Vazyme, Nanjing, China). Proteins were digested with trypsin (Promega) at an enzyme-to-substrate ratio of 1:50 (w/w) for 18 h at 37°C with digestion buffer (1 mM CaCl2, 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.6).  The resulting peptides were incubated overnight at 4 °C with streptavidin Sepharose 6FF beads (Smart-Lifesciences) under continuous rotation to enrich the NM-biotin-labeled peptides. Beads were subsequently washed three times with 100 mM phosphate buffer (pH 7.2) to remobe non-specifically bound peptides. Persulfides peptides were selectively eluted withby treatment with 10 mM dithiothreitol (DTT), while the NM-biotin-labelled thiol-containing peptides are retained in the beads. The eluted peptides were subsequently desalted, lyophilized, and subjected to LC-MS/MS analysis. Peptides were loaded onto a single reverse-phase column (75 µm ID × 360 µm OD) with a laser-pulled tip, home-packed with 30 cm C18 resin (ReproSil-Pur C18-AQ 1.9 µm resin; Dr. Maisch GmbH). The column was integrated into an Easy-nLC 1200 nano-HPLC system (Thermo Scientific) and subjected to a 120-minute gradient using the same buffer system as above. MS data were acquired using a Q-Exactive mass spectrometer (Thermo Scientific) operating in a data-dependent top-20 mode with a maximum injection time of 50 ms, a scan range of 300-1800 m/z, and an AGC target of 1e6. MS/MS was carried out via higher-energy collisional dissociation with a target value of 1e5 and a maximum injection time of 100 ms. Full MS and MS/MS scans were acquired at resolutions of 70,000 and 17,500, respectively, with a dynamic exclusion time of 15 sec.",
